    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0370" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve11p1/pg327"/>

                <head>102. Memorandum From Robert Hormats of the National Security Council Staff to
                    the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Scowcroft)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d102-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1976-09-20"
                        >September 20, 1976</date>.</dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>U.S. Assistance Program to Mexico</item>
                </list>
                <p>Agreement has been reached on the following help for Mexico:</p>
                <p>—a $600 million U.S. swap agreement with the Bank of Mexico;</p>
                <p>—a $1.2 billion IMF credit for Mexico.</p>
                <p>The swap is designed to help the Mexicans until the IMF credit can be made
                    available. Both should be useful in ameliorating current uncertainties in Mexico
                    which have precipitated a run on that country’s banks.</p>
                <p>This program will be announced in Washington at 11 a.m. today.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d102-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d102-f1-content">
                <p><seg type="summary">Summary: Hormats informed Scowcroft of an agreement under
                        which the United States would provide emergency financial assistance to
                        Mexico.</seg></p>
                <p><seg type="source">Source: Ford Library, National Security Adviser, NSC Staff for
                        International Economic Affairs Files, Convenience File, Box 2, Country File,
                        Mexico. Secret. Sent for information. In a September 20 memorandum, Simon
                        informed President Ford of the details of the financial assistance package
                        that would be provided to Mexico. (Ibid., Presidential Country Files for
                        Latin America, Box 5, Mexico—López Portillo Visit 3)</seg></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
